DELGROUP(8)                 System Manager's Manual                DELGROUP(8)

NAME
       delgroup - remove a group from the system

SYNOPSIS
       delgroup [--only-if-empty] GROUP
       delgroup --system [--only-if-empty] GROUP
       deluser USER GROUP

DESCRIPTION
       delgroup removes groups from the system.  It is the same program as
       deluser(8), invoked under the name delgroup so that group removal is
       the default action.

       delgroup GROUP
              Remove a group.  The group must not be the primary group of any
              user.

       delgroup --system GROUP
              Remove GROUP only if it is a system group (gid 100..999).

       deluser USER GROUP
              Remove an existing user from a group (a user cannot be removed
              from their primary group).

       Only the superuser may remove groups.

OPTIONS
       --system              only remove a system group
       --only-if-empty       only remove the group if it has no members
       --quiet, --verbose, --debug
                             adjust the amount of output
       --conf FILE           configuration file (accepted, unused)
       --help                display this help
       --version             display version

FILES
       /etc/group    group database

SEE ALSO
       deluser(8), adduser(8), addgroup(8), groups(1)

